cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, cite it using the metadata below, cite MoveAtlas
  (the data resource it reads), and cite the source paper of every dataset you
  use (each MoveAtlas data card carries its publications).
type: software
title: "MD_FM: a measured-body foundation model of abnormal human movement"
abstract: >-
  The code of the Movement Foundation Model program: one anonymous 3D body
  inferred from whatever was recorded, every MoveAtlas contract read as a
  physical measurement of that body through a differentiable sensor kernel,
  a healthy motion prior, unit-bearing pathology descriptors, and gate
  harnesses scored on subject-disjoint held-out splits.
authors:
  - family-names: Vasques
    given-names: Xavier
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-3752-5473"
version: 0.1.0.dev0
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/xaviervasques/mdfm"
keywords:
  - movement disorders
  - human movement
  - body model
  - inertial sensors
  - motion capture
  - foundation models
references:
  - type: software
    title: "MoveAtlas: the open atlas of movement data, human and animal"
    authors:
      - family-names: Vasques
        given-names: Xavier
    repository-code: "https://github.com/xaviervasques/moveatlas"
    license: BSD-3-Clause
